\ls12\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	a.	}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw4
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Heart Health\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl1
\f1\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Heart disease: is the leading cause of death for adults in the United States. Eating foods low in saturated fats and high in fiber, increasing access to low-sodium foods, and regular physical activity can help prevent high blood cholesterol and high blood pressure.\
\ls12\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone DASH Diet:
\f1\i0  The DASH diet, which is low in saturated fat and dietary cholesterol and rich in potassium, magnesium, calcium, and fiber, can help improve heart health.\
\ls12\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Limiting certain types of fats: 
\f1\i0 reducing trans-fat can improve your cholesterol and decrease the risk of stroke or heart attack.\
\pard\tx144\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	b.	}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw4
