\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl1
\f1\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Diet and Cancer Risk:
\f1\i0  An unhealthy diet can increase the risk of some cancers, particularly those related to being overweight and obese.\
\ls14\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Antioxidants
\f1\i0 : Consuming foods rich in antioxidants can lower cancer risk by protecting cells from damage caused by free radicals.\
\ls14\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Antioxidant-Rich Foods: 
\f1\i0 Fruits, vegetables, nuts, and legumes are good sources of antioxidants like beta-carotene, lycopene, and vitamins A, C, and E.\
\pard\tx144\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	c.	}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw4
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Weight Maintenance\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl1
\f1\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Food Choices for Health
\f0\i0\b :
\f1\b0  Foods like fruits, vegetables, and beans are lower in calories than processed foods.\
\ls16\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Benefits of Healthy Food Choices:
\f1\i0  Choosing these foods helps maintain a healthy weight and reduces the risk of chronic disease.\
\pard\tx144\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls17\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	d.	}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw4
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Overall Well-Being\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls18\ilvl1
\f1\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Mental Health Benefits:
\f1\i0  Foods rich in omega 3 fatty acids, vitamin b12, folate, and vitamin D are linked to reduced depression and anxiety.\
\ls18\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Cognitive Function Improvement:
\f1\i0  Diets high in fruits and vegetables are associated with enhanced brain function and memory.\
\ls18\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Body Image Enhancement:
\f1\i0  Healthy eating can contribute to a positive body image, leading to improved self-esteem.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls19\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Ways to Support Healthy Eating\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls20\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Healthy Eating Promotion in Schools:
\f1\b0  CDC\'92s Healthy Schools program promotes good nutrition in schools by providing guidelines and resources for healthier school meals, snacks, and water access.\
\ls20\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Workplace Wellness Initiatives:
\f1\b0  CDC encourages employers to offer healthier food options in cafeterias, snack shops, and vending machines, and supports breastfeeding mothers in the workplace.\
\ls20\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Improving Food Access in Underserved Communities:
\f1\b0  CDC funds programs to improve food systems in low-income and underserved areas by supporting food hubs, local stores, farmers\'92 markets, and bodegas.\
\ls20\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Low-Income Assistance Programs in the US:
\f1\b0  WIC and SNAP are two programs that provide nutrition education, food assistance, and financial support for low-income individuals and families.\
\ls20\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Healthy Eating Recommendations:
\f1\b0  Swap sugary drinks for water, reduce red meat consumption, prioritize lean proteins, and fill half your plate with fruits and vegetables.\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\sa360\partightenfactor0
