\ls21\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul What Makes a Healthy Diet?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \ulnone Healthy eating doesn\'92t involve any particular diet. Rather, it means prioritizing your health by fueling your body with a variety of nutrient-rich foods.\
\pard\tx144\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	a.	}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw4
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Nutrients\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl1
\f1\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Essential Nutrients:
\f1\b0  Nutrients that must be supplied by our diet because our bodies cannot make them, such as water.\
\ls22\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Non-essential Nutrients:
\f1\b0  Nutrients that our bodies can make, such as vitamin D.\
\ls22\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Macronutrients and Micronutrients:
\f1\b0  Macronutrients (carbohydrates, fat, and protein) are needed in large amounts, while micronutrients (vitamins and minerals) are needed in small amounts.\
\pard\tx144\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	b.	}\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw4
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Calories\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl1
\f1\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The energy released from our macronutrients can be measured in calories.\
\ls22\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Calorie Measurement:
\f1\b0  Calories are small units of energy, and food energy is typically measured in kilocalories (kcalories, or uppercase Calories - 1000 calories).\
\ls22\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrient Density
\f1\b0 : Nutrient-dense foods provide more beneficial nutrients relative to their calorie content.\
\ls22\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Energy Density: 
\f1\b0 Energy-dense foods are high in calories but low in nutrients, often referred to as \'93empty calories.\'94\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls23\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Creating Balance When Choosing Your Diet\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls24\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone A
\f0\b dequacy:
\f1\b0  Eating a variety of foods from all food groups ensures obtaining the right amounts of nutrients.\
\ls24\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Eating: 
\f1\b0 Consuming foods in reasonable  amounts, using portion control, and avoiding excessive intake of any single food.\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\sa360\partightenfactor0
\ls24\ilvl1\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Balance: 
\f1\b0 Prioritizing nutrient-dense foods over energy-dense foods to meet nutritional needs while allowing for occasional indulgence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl288\slmult1\sa100\partightenfactor0

