\cf2 Q: Which of the following steps of the scientific method is when you would make an educated guess about what would happen in an experiment? Hypothesis\
\
\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls25\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul The Science of Nutrition\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls25\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrition is the science that links food to health and includes how humans ingest, digest, absorb, transport, use, and excrete food.\
\ls25\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrition researchers use the scientific method to guide their work and help us make better choices for our health.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls26\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul The Scientific Method\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls27\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Steps\
\pard\tx432\tx824\pardeftab720\li824\fi-825\partightenfactor0
\ls27\ilvl3\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Propose a scientific or research question that will be interesting to investigate.\
\ls27\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Conduct research to examine other experiments that might impact the question.\
\ls27\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Formulate a hypothesis or an educated guess based on the research question.\
\ls27\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	4.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Design and conduct the experiment. A good design should take into account what has been done previously. Thus, a thorough review of methods and results published previously should be undertaken. This will help prevent making the same mistakes and save a lot of time performing the research.\
\ls27\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	5.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Analyze the the data and draw conclusions.\
\ls27\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	6.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone If the hypothesis is not supported, then a new hypothesis/research question should be created and an experiment conducted accordingly.\
\ls27\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	7.	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Communicate results (publish in peer reviewed journals).\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls27\ilvl1\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Experimental and Control Groups: To compare results and determine the effect of the treatment.\
\ls27\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Importance of Controlling Variables: To obtain the most accurate results by minimizing the influence of factors like athlete conditioning, age, or caffeine dosage.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls28\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul The Different Types of Studies\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls29\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Many nutrition studies are 
\f2\i observational
\f1\i0 , focusing on the occurrence, distribution, and contributing factors of health problems in populations.\
\ls29\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Epidemiology
\f0\i0\b : 
\f1\b0 the study of the occurrence, distribution, and factors that contribute to health problems in populations.\
\ls29\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone NHANES (National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey) and the Framingham Heart Study are examples of large-scale observational studies.\
\ls29\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Limitations of Observational Studies
\f1\i0 :\cb4  While valuable for identifying relationships, observational studies cannot establish cause and effect.\cb1 \
\ls29\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Scientific Method in Nutrition Science: Illustrated by the case of vitamin C and scurvy, where controlled trials and systematic reviews led to the discovery of the role of vitamin C in preventing scurvy.\
\ls29\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Interpreting Research Findings
\f0\i0\b : 
\f1\b0 Requires analyzing limitations, considering multiple high-quality studies, and relying on peer-reviewed research for evidence-based recommendations.\
\ls29\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Evidence-Based Practice in Nutrition: Nutrition and dietetics are evidence-based, meaning recommendations are based on the scientific method and constantly evolving with new research findings.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Vocab\
\pard\tx20\tx196\pardeftab720\li196\fi-197\sa80\partightenfactor0
\ls30\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrition
\f1\i0 \cb4 :\cb1  the sum of all processes involved in how organisms obtain nutrients, metabolize them, and use them to support all of life\'92s processes.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrients
\f1\i0 : A substance in food that can provide energy, contribute to body structure, and/or regulate body processes.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Health Claim
\f1\i0 : Claims that have been reviewed by the FDA and are allowed on food products showing that a food or food component may reduce the risk of a disease or a health-related condition.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Health Fraud
\f1\i0 : Fraud involving the selling of drugs, devices, foods, or cosmetics that have not been proven effective.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrition Misinformation
\f1\i0 : Information that is not supported by science and may be misleading or incomplete.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN)
\f1\i0 : A nutrition expert required to complete a specialized degree in dietetics, nutrition, public health, or other related sciences.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Diabetes
\f1\i0 : A chronic (long-lasting) health condition that affects how your body turns food into energy.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Food Aversions:
\f1\i0  A strong dislike of a specific food or foods.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Health Status:
\f1\i0  Refers to your medical conditions (both physical and mental health), claims experience, receipt of health care, medical history, genetic information, evidence of insurability, and disability.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Hypertension:
\f1\i0  Another name for high blood pressure. It can lead to severe health complications and increase the risk of heart disease, stroke, and sometimes death. Blood pressure is the force that a person's blood exerts against the walls of their blood vessels.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Palatability:
\f1\i0   Acceptable to the taste; sufficiently agreeable in flavor to be eaten.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Satiety:
\f1\i0  The quality or state of being fed or gratified to or beyond capacity.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Seasonality:
\f1\i0  Produce that is purchased and consumed around the time that it is harvested.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Antioxidants
\f1\i0 : Substances that can prevent or slow damage to cells caused by free radicals, unstable molecules produced by the body in response to environmental and other pressures.\
\pard\tx20\tx196\pardeftab720\li196\fi-197\sa80\partightenfactor0
\ls30\ilvl0
\f3 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Cardiovascular Disease (CVD)
\f3\i0 : A general term for conditions affecting the heart or blood vessels, typically associated with fatty deposits inside the arteries (atherosclerosis) and an increased risk of blood clots.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone DASH Diet
\f3\i0 : A flexible and balanced eating plan (Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension) designed to promote a heart-healthy eating style for life.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrient-Dense Food
\f3\i0 : Foods rich in vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients important for health, with minimal saturated fat, added sugars, and sodium.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Adequacy
\f3\i0 : The sufficient intake of essential nutrients needed to fulfill nutritional requirements for optimal health.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Balance
\f3\i0 : Consuming foods from multiple food groups to maintain optimal nutritional status.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Calorie
\f3\i0 : A unit of energy obtained from the food and beverages consumed.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Energy-Dense Food
\f3\i0 : Foods high in calories relative to the nutrients they contain.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Essential Nutrient
\f3\i0 : Nutrients vital for health, including vitamins, minerals, proteins, fats, water, and carbohydrates.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Macronutrient
\f3\i0 : Nutrients required in large amounts, such as carbohydrates, fats, and proteins.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Micronutrient
\f3\i0 : Vitamins and minerals essential for healthy development, disease prevention, and overall wellbeing.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Moderation
\f3\i0 : The practice of avoiding excess or extremes in consumption.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Epidemiology\cb1 :
\f3\i0  The study of the occurrence, distribution, and factors that contribute to health problems in populations.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey (NHANES):
\f3\i0  A program of studies designed to assess the health and nutritional status of adults and children in the United States.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Framingham Heart Study:
\f3\i0  A long-term, ongoing cardiovascular cohort study of residents of the city of Framingham, Massachusetts. Much of the knowledge concerning heart disease, such as the effects of diet, exercise, and common medications such as aspirin, is based on this longitudinal study.\
\ls30\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Scurvy
\f3\i0 : A disease caused by a deficiency of vitamin C, characterized by swollen bleeding gums and the opening of previously healed wounds, which particularly affected poorly nourished sailors until the end of the 18th century.\
\pard\tx20\tx196\pardeftab720\li196\fi-197\partightenfactor0
\ls30\ilvl0\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f4\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Evidence-Based
\f3\i0 : A practice that has been rigorously evaluated in experimental evaluations\'96like randomized controlled trials\'96and shown to make a positive, statistically significant difference in important outcomes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0

