\ls31\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul The Dietary Guidelines\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls31\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Food Group Plans: 
\f1\i0 Help build a balanced diet by selecting foods from different groups, each representing a unique set of nutrients.\
\ls31\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone USDA Dietary Guidelines
\f0\i0\b :
\f1\b0  Provide evidence-based recommendations for healthy eating patterns to promote health and prevent disease.\
\ls31\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 2020-2025 DGA Focus: 
\f1\i0 \'93Make Every Bite Count\'94 with four overarching guidelines: follow a healthy dietary pattern, customize nutrient-dense choices, focus on food group needs, and stay within calorie limits.\
\ls31\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Dietary Recommendations:
\f1\i0  Limit added sugars, saturated fat, sodium, and alcoholic beverages.\
\ls31\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Limits: 
\f1\i0 Less than 10% of calories from added sugars and saturated fat for ages 2+, less than 2,300mg sodium per day, and limit alcohol to 2 drinks/day for men and 1 drink/day for women.\
\ls31\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Overall Eating Pattern:
\f1\i0  Prioritize nutrient-rich foods, with limited room for added sugars, saturated fats, and alcohol.\
\ls31\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The Dietary Guidelines framework purposely provides recommendations by food groups and subgroups - not specific foods and beverages - to avoid being prescriptive. This framework approach ensures that people can \'93make it their own\'94 by selecting healthy foods, beverages, meals, and snacks specific to their needs and preferences.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls32\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	2.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul The Three USDA Food Patterns \
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab720\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls33\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Dietary Guidelines Recommendations
\f0\i0\b :
\f1\b0  Provide guidance on healthy eating across the lifespan.\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls33\ilvl1\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone USDA Food Patterns
\f0\i0\b :
\f1\b0  Identify daily amounts of foods from five major food groups and their subgroups to help individuals carry out Dietary Guidelines recommendations.\
\ls33\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Three USDA Food Patterns:
\f1\i0  Healthy U.S.-Style Pattern, Healthy Vegetarian Pattern, and Healthy Mediterranean-Style Pattern.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls34\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Tools for Developing Dietary Patterns\
\pard\tx216\tx432\pardeftab560\li432\fi-432\partightenfactor0
\ls35\ilvl1
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Balanced Diet: 
\f1\i0 All food groups are essential, and daily selections should be made from each, with amounts varying based on individual energy needs.\
\ls35\ilvl1\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone USDA Food Patterns:
\f1\i0  Recommended amounts and limits are set at 12 calorie levels, ranging from 1,000 to 3,200 calories, to meet the nutritional needs of individuals of different ages and activity levels.\
