\ls52\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	1.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Introduction to the Six Classes of Nutrients\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\partightenfactor0
\ls52\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrients are substances required by our body to perform its basic functions.\
\ls52\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrients provide energy (calories), help us build muscle and bone, and regulate chemical processes, essential functions for humans to maintain life.\
\ls52\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 6 nutrient classes: \cb4 carbohydrates, lipids, proteins, water, vitamins, and minerals. \cb1 \
\ls52\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Two main groups: macronutrients & micronutrients. Macronutrients: carbohydrates, fat, protein, and water. Micronutrients: vitamins and minerals. Foods also contain non-nutrients like preservatives or antioxidants.\
