\ls66\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Minerals are used for fluid balance, enzymes, synthesis of hormones, and protecting against free radicals. \
\ls66\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Minerals are broken down into trace minerals and major minerals. \
\ls66\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Trace: iron, zinc, iodine, selenium, copper, manganese, fluoride, and chromium. \
\ls66\ilvl2\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Major:
\f1\i0 \cb4  sodium, chloride, potassium, calcium, phosphorus, magnesium, and sulfur.\cb1 \uc0\u8232 \

