\ls72\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone The second food group is vegetables. Vegetables provide many important nutrients, such as potassium, folate, fiber, vitamin A, and vitamin C. \
\ls72\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Can reduce risk of heart disease, heart attack, and stroke. \
\ls72\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone 5 main groups: dark green, red and orange, beans and peas, starchy, and other.\
\ls72\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Greens offer antioxidants, magnesium, calcium, and iron. \
\ls72\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Red and orange vegetables: vitamin A, potassium, and fiber. \
\ls72\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Beans, peas, and lentils are good sources of B vitamins, iron, magnesium, and protein. \
\ls72\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Starchy vegetables are the most consumed and include foods like potatoes, corn, lima beans, green peas, and string beans.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
