\ls74\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Bulk of the diet and can be divided into two groups: whole and refined. Whole grains contain the whole part of the grain, including the bran, germ, and endosperm. This makes it so that whole grains provide more nutrients, such as fiber, iron, and B vitamins. \
\ls74\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Refined grains remove the bran and germ leaving only the endosperm increasing shelf life but removing most nutrients. These grains are typically enriched to add back some B vitamins and iron to the grain. \
\ls74\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Whole grains include whole-wheat flour, bulgur, oatmeal, whole grain cornmeal, and brown rice. \
\ls74\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Refined grains include white flour, corn grits, white bread, and white rice.\
\ls74\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone At least half of the grains you eat should be whole grains.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls75\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	5.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Proteins\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\partightenfactor0
\ls76\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone High-protein foods help the body build and maintain muscles, skin, blood, and other tissues. They also have important vitamins and minerals, like iron.\
\ls76\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Animal meats are recommended to be either lean or low-fat. To be lean or low-fat, the calories from fat should be 30% or lower.\
\ls76\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Proteins are the building blocks of the muscles and tissues and requires the nutrients from the other food groups to function properly.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
