\ls81\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Limit sodium intake to less than 2,300 mg per day to reduce the risk of high blood pressure and cardiovascular disease.\
\ls81\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Macronutrient Recommendations: Fat should make up 20\'9635%, carbohydrates should make up 45-65%, and protein should make up 10-35% of total calories.\
\ls81\ilvl2\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Dietary Reference Intakes (DRIs): Understand the four DRIs: RDA (average daily intake sufficient for nearly all healthy individuals), EAR (estimated average requirement for half the healthy individuals in a group), AI (adequate intake), and UL (tolerable upper intake level).\cb1 \
\ls81\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Daily Value (DV): Used to estimate how a food can fit into a 2,000-calorie daily diet, with \'93low\'94 DV being 5% or less and \'93high\'94 DV being 20% or more.\
