\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Healthy Diet Principles: Balance, adequacy, calorie control, nutrient density, moderation, and variety.\
\ls86\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Balance in Diet: Consuming the right amounts of macronutrients (proteins, fats, carbohydrates) and micronutrients (vitamins and minerals).\
\ls86\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Adequacy in Diet: Providing sufficient energy and nutrients for optimal growth, maintenance, and repair of the body.\
\ls86\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Calorie Control: Involves consuming the right amount of calories for the body\'92s needs, avoiding excess intake.\
\ls86\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrient Density: Focuses on choosing foods that are rich in nutrients but relatively low in calories.\
\ls86\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Variety: Emphasizes the importance of incorporating a diverse range of foods and cuisines into one\'92s diet.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls87\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	3.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Basics for Planning a Diet Using MyPlate\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\partightenfactor0
\ls88\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Some of the basics for planning a diet using MyPlate are:\
\pard\tx720\tx936\pardeftab720\li936\fi-936\partightenfactor0
\ls88\ilvl3\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Fill half of your plate with fruits and vegetables. Vary your choices to get the benefit of as many different vegetables and fruits as you can.\
\ls88\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Fill a quarter of your plate with grains. Half of your daily grain intake should be whole grains.\
\ls88\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Select a variety of protein foods to improve nutrient intake and promote health benefits. When choosing meat, select lean cuts.\
\ls88\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Choose low-fat or nonfat dairy products, such as cheese and yogurt. Low-fat and nonfat products contain the same amount of calcium and other essential nutrients as whole-milk products, but with much less fat and calories.\
\ls88\ilvl3\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Oils in moderation. Oil contain more healthful unsaturated fats compared to solid fats like butter.\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\partightenfactor0
\ls88\ilvl2\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Prioritize nutrient-dense foods to help you achieve your nutrition goals.\
\pard\tx20\tx360\pardeftab720\li360\fi-360\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls89\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	4.	}\kerning1\expnd1\expndtw5
\up0 \nosupersub \ul Diet Planning Tools in MyPlate\
\pard\tx360\tx576\pardeftab720\li576\fi-576\partightenfactor0
\ls90\ilvl2
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone When planning a healthy meal using MyPlate dietary guidelines, your plate should consist of about 30% vegetables, 20% fruit, 30% grains, and 20% protein and about a glass or dairy.\
\ls90\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone At least half of your grain should be whole grain, 100% fruit juice should only make up half of your fruits, and 100% vegetable juice should only make up half of your vegetables.\
\ls90\ilvl2\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Vary the types of vegetables and proteins consumed from meal to meal. Many Americans consume the daily recommended amount of meat, poultry, and eggs, they do not typically eat enough seafood, seeds, nuts, and soy products. Therefore, special attention should be given to these types of protein.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

