\ls91\ilvl0
\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Nutrients: 
\f1\i0 Substances required by our body to perform its basic functions.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Complex Carbohydrates:
\f1\i0  Long chains of simple sugars that can be unbranched or branched. These are called polysaccharides.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Amino Acids:
\f1\i0  Simple subunits composed of carbon, oxygen, hydrogen, and nitrogen.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Enzymes:
\f1\i0  Proteins that catalyze chemical reactions.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone MyPlate: 
\f1\i0 A nutritional food guide, developed by the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA).\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Adequate Intake (AI): 
\f1\i0 A value based on observed or experimentally determined approximations of nutrient intake by a group (or groups) of healthy people; used when an RDA cannot be determined.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Estimated Average Requirement (EAR):
\f1\i0  A nutrient intake value that is estimated to meet the requirement of half the healthy individuals in a group; should be used as dietary intake goals for health.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA)
\f1\i0 : The average daily dietary intake is sufficient to meet the nutrient requirement of nearly all (about 97%) of healthy individuals in a group.\
\ls91\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Serving Size:
\f1\i0  The amount of a food\'a0that is customarily eaten at one time, and all of the nutrition information on the label is based on one serving of the food.\
\pard\tx20\tx196\pardeftab720\li196\fi-197\partightenfactor0
\ls91\ilvl0\cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f2\i \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL):
\f1\i0  The highest level of daily nutrient intake that is likely to pose no risk of adverse health effects to almost all individuals in the general population; a level that is avoided to prevent negative health effects.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
