\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone ATP is an 
\f0\b energy-carrying
\f1\b0  molecule found in the cells of all living things. ATP captures chemical energy obtained from the breakdown of food molecules and releases it to fuel other cellular processes. ATP does not store chemical energy long term; carbohydrates, such as glycogen, and fats are examples of storage molecules. When energy is needed by cells, the cells convert energy from storage molecules into ATP. ATP then serves as a carrier and can deliver energy to places within the cell where it is needed.\uc0\u8232 \u8232 {{\NeXTGraphic 5__#$!@%!#__pastedGraphic.png \width7120 \height5040 \appleattachmentpadding0 \appleembedtype0 \appleaqc
