\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Fiber: A complex carbohydrate. The human body cannot break down most fibers. Fibers are found in fruits, vegetables, nuts, seeds, beans, and whole grains.\
\ls253\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Insoluble Fiber: Fiber that adds bulk to your stool and can improve bowel-related health problems, like constipation or hemorrhoids.\
\ls253\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Soluble Fiber: Fiber that attracts water and turns to gel during digestion, which in turn slows digestion and helps feed the good bacteria in your intestines.\
\ls253\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Starch: Complex carbohydrates, which are made of lots of simple sugars combined. These include bread, cereal, pasta, and some vegetables such as potatoes, peas, and corn.\
\pard\tx20\tx196\pardeftab720\li196\fi-197\partightenfactor0
