\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Artificial Sweeteners: Substances that are used instead of sucrose (table sugar) to sweeten foods and beverages. They are also called sugar substitutes.\
\ls271\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Diabetes: A disease in which your blood glucose, or blood sugar, levels are too high.\
\ls271\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Gestational Diabetes: When a pregnant woman gets diabetes.\
\ls271\ilvl0\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Insulin: A hormone that prompts cells to absorb sugar out of your blood for energy or storage.\
\ls271\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Insulin Resistance: When the body can\'92t make enough insulin or can\'92t properly use the insulin it makes. It causes blood sugar and insulin levels to stay high long after eating.\
\ls271\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Ketosis: When the body uses fat for energy because there are not enough carbohydrates from food for the body to use for energy.\
\ls271\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Prediabetes: When a person\'92s blood glucose, or blood sugar, levels are higher than normal but not high enough to be called diabetes.\
\ls271\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Type 1 Diabetes: When one\'92s body does not make insulin so you must take insulin for your cells to use glucose properly. It is also known as insulin dependent diabetes mellitus (IDDM).\
\pard\tx20\tx196\pardeftab720\li196\fi-197\partightenfactor0
\ls271\ilvl0\cf2 \cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Type 2 Diabetes: When a person\'92s body does not make or use insulin well. This can be treated with medication but can progress into being insulin dependent. It is the more common type and is also known as non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa360\partightenfactor0
