\f1\b0 \cf2 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Atherosclerosis: The hardening and narrowing of arteries.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Blood Cholesterol: A waxy, fat-like substance made by your liver.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Cardiovascular Disease (CVD): A general term for conditions affecting the heart or blood vessels.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Congestive Heart Failure: A serious condition in which the heart doesn\'92t pump blood as efficiently as it should.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Heart Attack: When a part of the heart muscle doesn\'92t get enough blood. It usually happens when blood flow to a section of the heart is cut off due to a blood clot. It is also called a myocardial infarction.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Hyperlipidemia: increased level of lipids, cholesterol, and triglycerides in one\'92s blood.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Ischemic Stroke: when a blood clot blocks or narrows an artery leading to the brain.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\cb4 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Lipoprotein: Bad cholesterol in one's blood.\
\ls306\ilvl0\cb1 \up0 \nosupersub \ulnone {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\up0 \nosupersub \ulnone Overweight: Weight that is higher than what is considered healthy for a given height.\
